{"name":"Tumbling Tumbleweed","hex":"#cebf9c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tumbling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of tumble"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of something that tumbles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tumbling"},{"term":"tumbleweed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant which habitually breaks away from its roots once dry, forming a light, rolling mass which is driven by the wind from place to place; as Russian thistle, wild indigo, witch grass, Amaranthus albus, etc.","One of the dried-out, seed-dispersing, globular forms of such plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tumbleweed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tumbling Tumbleweeds","blocks":[{"text":"\"Tumbling Tumbleweeds\" is a Western music song composed by Bob Nolan, a founding member of the Sons of the Pioneers. Nolan wrote the song in the early 1930s while he was working as a caddy and living in Los Angeles. It was first recorded by the Sons of the Pioneers in 1934, and it became one of the most famous songs associated with the group. Originally titled \"Tumbling Leaves\", the song was reworked into the title \"Tumbling Tumbleweeds\" and into more widespread fame with the 1935 film of the same name starring Gene Autry. Members of the Western Writers of America chose it as one of the Top 100 Western songs of all time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4b/Tumbling_tumbleweeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumbling_Tumbleweeds"},{"title":"Tumbleweed","blocks":[{"text":"A tumbleweed is any structural part of the above-ground anatomy of a number of species of plants. It is a diaspore that, once mature and dry, detaches from its root or stem and rolls due to the force of the wind. It is also the name used for these types of plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Tumbleweed_in_motion.webm/330px--Tumbleweed_in_motion.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumbleweed"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg/500px-Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg/1280px-Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg/500px-Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young plant blooming in the Mojave Desert in April, after an extremely wet winter season","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATumbleweed_Blooming.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salsola_tragus_tumbleweed.jpg/500px-Salsola_tragus_tumbleweed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salsola_tragus_tumbleweed.jpg/500px-Salsola_tragus_tumbleweed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Salsola tragus tumbleweed caught against a fence","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalsola_tragus_tumbleweed.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Amaranthus_albus_%288186656590%29.jpg/500px-Amaranthus_albus_%288186656590%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Amaranthus_albus_%288186656590%29.jpg/1280px-Amaranthus_albus_%288186656590%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Amaranthus_albus_%288186656590%29.jpg/500px-Amaranthus_albus_%288186656590%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Amaranthus albus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmaranthus_albus_(8186656590).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Brunsvigia_bosmaniae02.jpg/500px-Brunsvigia_bosmaniae02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Brunsvigia_bosmaniae02.jpg/500px-Brunsvigia_bosmaniae02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brunsvigia bosmaniae in flower in the veld, showing the globular umbels of tumbleweed Amaryllidaceae","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrunsvigia_bosmaniae02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/2_Salsola_on_fence.jpg/500px-2_Salsola_on_fence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/2_Salsola_on_fence.jpg/1280px-2_Salsola_on_fence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/2_Salsola_on_fence.jpg/500px-2_Salsola_on_fence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mass of Salsola tumbleweeds caught behind a fence","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2_Salsola_on_fence.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Anastatica_hierochuntica.jpg/500px-Anastatica_hierochuntica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Anastatica_hierochuntica.jpg/500px-Anastatica_hierochuntica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anastatica, a North African desert tumbleweed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnastatica_hierochuntica.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Selaginella_lepidophylla_trocken.jpeg/500px-Selaginella_lepidophylla_trocken.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Selaginella_lepidophylla_trocken.jpeg/500px-Selaginella_lepidophylla_trocken.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Selaginella lepidophylla, a North American desert tumbleweed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASelaginella_lepidophylla_trocken.jpeg"}],"sounds":{"tumbling":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/En-us-tumbling.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/57/En-us-tumbling.ogg/En-us-tumbling.ogg.mp3"}],"tumbleweed":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fc/En-us-tumbleweed.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fc/En-us-tumbleweed.ogg/En-us-tumbleweed.ogg.mp3"}]}}}